    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "\nSherry FitzGerald are delighted to present to the market this charming two-bedroom end-of-terrace property.\nNo. 1 Bishop Street is an attractive red-brick residence offering bright, well-proportioned accommodation that has been tastefully modernised while retaining its character and charm. Presented in very good condition throughout, this appealing city home is ready for immediate occupation, making it an ideal purchase for first-time buyers, investors, or those seeking to downsize to a convenient city-centre location.\nSituated in Limerick's historic Medieval Quarter, No. 1 enjoys a quiet yet highly convenient setting in the heart of Limerick City. The property is just a short stroll from the city centre and benefits from an excellent range of amenities on its doorstep, including restaurants, cafés, bars, shops and leisure facilities. Some of Limerick's most renowned educational institutions, including the Limerick School of Art and Design and the UL City Campus, are all within walking distance. The landmark Opera Square development is also located just moments away.\nUpon entering No. 1 Bishop Street, you are greeted by a bright and welcoming reception room featuring an attractive open fireplace, creating a warm focal point to the home. To the rear, the kitchen is fitted with a range of modern units and offers direct access to the private rear patio area. The patio further benefits from valuable side access leading onto Exchange Street, providing excellent convenience. Also located on the ground floor is the family bathroom, which is fitted with a bath.\nUpstairs, there are two spacious bedrooms, both of which enjoy excellent natural light and one main bathroom with a free standing shower.\n\nAll contents, fixtures and fittings included in the sale. \n\nAccommodation: Entrance Hall, Living Room, Kitchen, Bathroom, and Two Bedrooms.\n\nServices: GFCH, Double-Glazed Windows, On-Street Parking (residential permit available from Limerick City & County Council), Side Access, Alarm.\n\nFloor Area: Approx. 55 sq.m. (592 sq.ft.)"
      },
